## Conditions

### 1. License Preservation (File-Level Copyleft)

This license applies at the file level. Any file that is part of the Software,
or that is a direct modification of a file that is part of the Software, must
remain under this license in all copies and distributions, without exception.
You may not relicense any such file under different terms.

This license notice and copyright notice must be retained in all copies or
substantial portions of the Software.

New files you create that are separate from the Software's original files
("Additions") are not subject to this license, unless Section 4 applies.

### 2. Internal Use

You may use the Software internally within your organization for any purpose,
including commercial purposes, without any obligation to make your source code
publicly available.

### 3. Building on Top (Additions)

You may write Additions — software that uses, calls, links to, or builds upon
the Software — without being required to open source your Additions and without
being required to apply this license to your Additions, provided that:

a) All original Software files, and any modifications you make to those files,
   remain under this license (per Section 1).

b) You are not engaging in commercial use as defined in Section 4.

### 4. Commercial Use — Open Source Requirement

If you make money from the Software in any form — including but not limited to
selling the Software, hosting it as a paid service (SaaS), or charging users
for access to a product or service that is substantially based on the Software
— you must:

a) Make the complete corresponding source code of all original Software files,
   including all modifications you have made to them, publicly available under
   this license.

b) Make the complete corresponding source code of all Additions that are part
   of the commercial product or service publicly available. You may choose any
   OSI-approved open source license for your Additions.

c) Display a prominent notice to users indicating where the source code can
   be obtained.

Internal commercial use (Section 2) is exempt from this requirement.

### 5. No AI Training Use

The Software, including any Derivative Works or modifications, may not be used,
directly or indirectly, for any of the following purposes:

a) Training, fine-tuning, or improving any machine learning model or artificial
   intelligence system.

b) Inclusion in any dataset used for machine learning, artificial intelligence,
   natural language processing, code generation, or data mining.

c) Any purpose that primarily serves the development or improvement of AI or
   ML systems.

Any violation of this condition constitutes a breach of this License and
immediately terminates all rights granted herein.

